        "head_rest_blender": [
          0.6588,
          0.3056,
          0.8783
        ],
        "axes": "+Y barrel (along the hand, ahead in the hold), +Z weapon top (up in the hold)"
      },
      "runtime_contract": {
        "clip_names": "looping clips carry a \"-loop\" suffix (Godot imports them as Idle / IdleArmed / Walk / WalkArmed with loop LINEAR); look clips up by both names",
        "armed": "IdleArmed / WalkArmed when the unit holds a one-handed weapon; Attack starts and ends in that hold; attach the weapon to the weapon_r bone (+Y barrel, +Z top)",
        "walk": "in place; move the unit 2 m per Walk cycle (0.8 s) on straight tiles (8 OXCE walk phases per tile); the serpent body slides along its own path, the torso bobs and surges with the sprite",
        "turn_to_attacker": null,
        "hit": "non-lethal: play Hit<variant> (0.3 s directional recoil; variant from the shot direction relative to the facing, ragdoll.handoff.variant_rule); no turn",
        "death": "user decisions 2026-10-02: play Death<variant> (0.133 s snappy recoil away from the shot; no turn, no crumple); on its last frame start the ragdoll with that variant's velocities (ragdoll.handoff.variants), the ground-clearance lift, a small push along the shot on spine_02 / spine_03 / head, the whole-body twist toward the shooter (ragdoll.handoff.twist_toward_shooter: rigid rotation of all bodies about the vertical, 0 for a frontal shot, full from behind) and the per-death variation; settle-and-freeze with the settle-assist rule; DeathBaked is the no-physics fallback (DeathFront then falls backward over the coil)",
        "blood": "every shot: ray-cast against the unit, a wound decal at the hit point on the hit bone (BoneAttachment3D, cull mask = the unit's own visual layer, capped) with drip runs growing down the surface (opus-v3: a ragged entry hole, wound_decals.variants picked at random per hit + a random roll) and the hit spray from the hit point (blood.json wound_decals, spray.runtime; opus-v3: the emitter origin_inset_m under the skin, billboard pulled depth_pull_m toward the camera); at death floor splatter decals; pool under the frozen corpse inside the death tile. No UV0 wound overlay",
        "blood_spray": "the spray starts on the visible skin at the hit point (nudged ~4 mm out along the normal) and flies BACK toward the shooter: normalize(-shot travel + surface normal) in the spray.runtime cone (user correction 2026-10-02)"
      },
